{"id": "2025-11-13-gcb-2025-land-sink-recovery", "result": "corrected", "evidence": [{"doc": 1, "quote": "The 20th edition of the annual Global Carbon Budget report, published today, also finds that the land carbon sink – the portion of human-caused CO2 emissions absorbed by plants and soils – appears to have recovered to its pre-El Niño strength after two unusually weak years."}, {"doc": 1, "quote": "And while the land sink has recovered to its pre-El Niño strength in 2025, aided by relatively low global fire CO2 emissions, it will continue to gradually weaken as global temperatures rise."}, {"doc": 2, "quote": "13 November 2025 0:01"}], "fetched": [{"doc": 1, "url": "https://www.carbonbrief.org/analysis-fossil-fuel-co2-emissions-to-set-new-record-in-2025-as-land-sink-recovers/", "status": 200, "ok": true, "chars": 28205, "fetched_at": "2026-10-12T16:53:06+00:00", "sha256": "29967da1aa77a21fe4bd8db17d7bc407121bf659a5bb9a22db517a6502a76bf9"}, {"doc": 2, "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260107175112id_/https://www.carbonbrief.org/analysis-fossil-fuel-co2-emissions-to-set-new-record-in-2025-as-land-sink-recovers/", "status": 200, "ok": true, "chars": 33988, "fetched_at": "2026-10-12T16:53:24+00:00", "sha256": "0e72209d514c231c60d9cf61574166bbd0a52021f1140e2c34c094722118fd9d"}]}
